    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0252" n="252" xml:id="pg252"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dayton to Mr.
                            Seward</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract.]</note>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 10, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I herewith enclose to you a copy and translation of a communication recently
                    received by me from Mr. Thouvenel on the subject of the execution of the
                    convention as to maritime rights. It contains nothing that I have not referred
                    to before, but it is evident he wanted to put the specific grounds of exception
                    to an unconditional exception of the treaty on record.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>With much respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d153-a1.xml" xpointer="d153-a1"/>
            </div>
